  "summary_en": "Health NZ guidance for staff on generative AI and LLMs. It recommends caution, bars entering identifiable patient or organisational data into unapproved tools and bars using them for clinical decisions. It also sets out risks: privacy, inaccuracy, bias, opacity, Māori data sovereignty, language gaps and IP.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Staff and contractors must not enter personal, confidential or sensitive information into unapproved LLMs.",
   "Generative AI must not be used for clinical decisions or personalised patient advice.",
   "Users must verify outputs and acknowledge use of generative AI.",
   "Plans to use generative AI must be cleared via advice from Health NZ.",
   "Risks include privacy breaches, hallucination, bias, lack of transparency, Māori data sovereignty and IP infringement."
  ],
